      "[Signal 1 - GSE351727 CAF-derived ANP32A drives cisplatin resistance in ESCC, Homo sapiens, score 6, n=6, pdat 2026/10/25 = FRESHEST NOVEL accession of the day]: the strongest new refractory-cancer signal in today's scan because it identifies the CARRIER of the resistant phenotype rather than the phenotype itself. CAFs elevate glutathione abundance in ESCC cells via extracellular-vesicle-mediated communication; proteomic profiling of CAF EVs plus prognostic analysis nominated ANP32A as the effector; ANP32A depletion in CAFs abolished the EV capacity to raise GSH, suppress ROS and lipid peroxidation, and protect ESCC cells from cisplatin cytotoxicity. Mechanistically ANP32A binds ANXA2 and STAT3, and that interaction is required for efficient STAT3 activation; ChIP-based analysis then identified SLC29A4 (PMAT) as the downstream STAT3 target essential for ANP32A-dependent GSH homeostasis and cisplatin resistance. Deletion mapping pinned amino acids 123-161 of ANP32A as the region required for ANXA2 association and the full drug-resistant phenotype - which converts a correlative biomarker into a druggable interface and a candidate peptide-mimic / small-molecule angle. Critically, tumor-targeted tetrahedral DNA nanostructures delivering siANP32A lowered GSH, raised lipid peroxidation and suppressed ESCC xenograft growth, so the entry point is not only diagnostic. Why it matters for BB: this is exactly the shape of the refractory-cancer brief Brown Biotech sells - a stromal-immune-metabolic escape mechanism with a named target, a defined interaction domain, and an in-vivo delivery proof of concept - and it is human material, so the reasoning layer can be validated against clinical relevance immediately. It also reinforces id:135 and id:136's carrier-and-vehicle thesis: here the carrier is the CAF-derived EV, the vehicle is the DNA nanostructure, and the target sits in the stromal cell rather than in the tumor cell that actually fails to respond.",
